		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Updated COLLADA Physics viewer/test files]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2950#p2950"><![CDATA[
Very basic Win32 glut demo that imports and exports (press 'e' during simulation) COLLADA Physics files using <a href="http://sourceforge.net/project/showfiles.php?group_id=157838" class="postlink">COLLADA 1.4.1 DOM 1.2.0</a><br><br>3 different COLLADA physics test files are created in Maya 8 (PhysX plugin), <a href="http://www.codesuppository.blogspot.com" class="postlink">CreateDynamics</a> (thanks <a href="http://www.ageia.com" class="postlink">http://www.ageia.com</a> ) and Blender 2.42.<br><br>Download 1Mb zipfile with win32 exe + 3 COLLADA .dae files here:<br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pub/test/physics/Collada%20Physics/COLLADA1.4.1PhysicsTests.zip" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pu ... sTests.zip</a> <br><br>On request Mac OS X universal binary can be provided/uploaded too.<br><br>Feedback welcome!<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Wed Dec 20, 2006 10:35 pm</p><hr />
